<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements for the PyInstaller sidecar, and only for it.

  The hardened runtime requires every library a process loads to be signed by
  the same team. A PyInstaller onefile binary unpacks its own Python.framework
  into a temporary directory at launch and loads it from there — signed by
  PyInstaller's build, not by us — so the loader refuses it and the daemon dies
  before it opens a socket. That is the failure documented in
  scripts/macos-sign-and-dmg.sh as "different Team IDs".

  `disable-library-validation` is the entitlement Apple provides for exactly
  this case. It is narrow: it lets this one binary load libraries from another
  team, and grants nothing else. It does not disable the hardened runtime, does
  not allow unsigned executable memory, and does not apply to the app bundle —
  which is signed without it.

  Nothing else is listed on purpose. `allow-unsigned-executable-memory` and
  `allow-dyld-environment-variables` are the two usually pasted in alongside
  this one; both weaken the runtime further and neither was needed here, which
  was established by trying without them rather than by assuming.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
